<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Apps on Matthew</title><link>http://localhost:1313/tags/apps/</link><description>Recent content in Apps on Matthew</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 06 May 2024 18:10:38 -0700</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="http://localhost:1313/tags/apps/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Tools</title><link>http://localhost:1313/posts/tools/</link><pubDate>Mon, 06 May 2024 18:10:38 -0700</pubDate><guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/tools/</guid><description>&lt;h4 id="apache-guacamole-clientless-remote-desktop-gateway"&gt;Apache Guacamole (Clientless remote desktop gateway)&lt;/h4&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Supporting standard remote protocols like VNC, RDP, and SSH.&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://guacamole.apache.org/"&gt;https://guacamole.apache.org/&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;img src="images/guacamole.png" alt="Apache Guacamole"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h4 id="googles-dig-webapp-dns-lookup"&gt;Google&amp;rsquo;s Dig webapp (DNS lookup)&lt;/h4&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Tool for interrogating DNS name servers.&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://toolbox.googleapps.com/apps/dig/"&gt;https://toolbox.googleapps.com/apps/dig/&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;img src="images/google-dig.png" alt="Google Dig "&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h4 id="obsidian"&gt;Obsidian&lt;/h4&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Flexible writing application using markdown, a non-propietary language.&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://obsidian.md/"&gt;https://obsidian.md/&lt;/a&gt;&#10;&lt;img src="images/obsidian.png" alt="Obsidian"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h4 id="kompose"&gt;Kompose&lt;/h4&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Docker compose to Kubernetes/Openshift conversion tool.&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://kompose.io/"&gt;https://kompose.io/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;$ kompose convert -f compose.yaml&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;$ kubectl apply -f .&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;$ kubectl get pods&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;NAME READY STATUS RESTARTS AGE&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;frontend-591253677-5t038 1/1 Running &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; 10s&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;redis-leader-2410703502-9hshf 1/1 Running &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; 10s&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;redis-replica-4049176185-hr1lr 1/1 Running &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; 10s&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;sub&gt;While you can get away without a version tag in your compose.yml file for modern docker ce, you will get a complaint from this tool unless you put in a &lt;code&gt;version:&lt;/code&gt; tag&lt;/sub&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>